Expected elements: MISSING — a timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace

That absence is finding #1, it is P1, and my rating is 4. The identity bar carries the back-link, hash, `Partial`, `block 101`, four button pairs, `128 / 1315`, the phase rail, `NOIR` and two icon actions — but no track, no ticks, no playhead anywhere between the controls and the rail, and no time surface in any pane. The `1…8` strip in the Code pane is a scrubber over one loop, not over the trace. The fraction is the position *readout*, which the block lists as a separate item.

Typographically the page is otherwise competent: one consistent pane-title level, right-aligned comma-grouped opcode counts in the Call Trace, right-aligned tabular values in Values. The failures are all at the edges of the type system.

The hierarchy is inverted at the top: the provenance prose is the largest, loosest text on the screen, senior to every pane title. Truncation is the worst offender — three strategies for one data type (middle-ellipsis in the bar, hard wrap with two-character orphans in the Transaction pane, right-ellipsis that eats the filename in the Call Trace), plus source lines cut at the pane border with no ellipsis at all.

Highest-priority fixes: (1) restore a trace timeline; (2) settle one identifier-truncation rule and apply it in all three places; (3) tighten the Code pane's ~1.85 leading.

Rating: 4/10

